A machine that declares no `artifact:` is addressed by a file named per run: its `## State` block
says so, and both the frontier line and its `Advance:` invocation take `{path}` as the file and
name `--playbook`, since no path pattern can infer the machine.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-targetless/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-targetless
title: Targetless
---

Preamble prose for the targetless playbook.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-targetless/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  a: []

states:
  main:
    initial: reviewing
    statuses:
      reviewing:
        transitions:
          - to: reviewed
            when: the review is written
      reviewed: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-targetless/a/prompt.md --
---
name: a
summary: a summary
---

a body
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-targetless
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
Preamble prose for the targetless playbook.

## Playbook Steps

Execute the steps in the most effective order considering their dependencies.

| Step | Dependencies | Summary | Review gate |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `a` | — | a summary | — |

## State

Run state is persisted in artifacts under the run workdir. Only `booping transition` writes it — never hand-edit an artifact's `status`.

Read the whole run's frontier before starting or resuming:

```
booping state {path} --playbook fx-targetless
```

### State: main

- Referenced by: outer graph
- Artifact: named per run — pass it as `{path}` on every call
- Initial status: `reviewing`
- Advance: `booping transition {path} <to> --playbook fx-targetless`

| Status | To | When | Gates |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `reviewing` | `reviewed` | the review is written | — |
| `reviewed` | *(terminal)* | — | — |

## Step: A
Instructions:
- Summary: a summary

Run `booping render-playbook fx-targetless --step a` for content.
